  "worked_solution": "The range of $\\theta =\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061x$ is given by\n\n$$\n-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<\\theta <\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nNote that the angle $\\theta $ spans the first and fourth quadrants.\n\nSince $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$ is positive, our answer is an angle that lies in the first quadrant, where the tangent is positive.\n\nFrom the special values of the trigonometric functions, we know that \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{6})=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}.\n$$\n\nSince $\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ is an angle in the first quadrant that lies within the range of $arctan,$ we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}})=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.\n$$",
